# Raw captures are EVIDENCE — store them byte-exact.
#
# Git's default text handling would normalise line endings on checkout, so a
# teammate cloning this repo would get different bytes than the board actually
# wrote. That silently breaks two things:
#
#   * validate_integrity.py's SHA-256 manifest (hashes would not match)
#   * byte-for-byte provenance, which is the whole point of keeping raw CSVs
#
# `-text` disables all line-ending conversion for these paths.
tools/exports/**/*.csv -text
tools/exports/**/*.csv.orig -text

# Analysis outputs are regenerated, not evidence — normal text handling is fine
# for the CSVs, but the plots must never be touched.
*.png binary
*.pdf binary
